From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:01:34 +0400
Subject: drm/nouveau/dispnv50: support HDMI deep color

TMDS output stays at 8 bpc even when the GPU and sink support deep color.
Select a supported HDMI depth at atomic check, allowing 12 bpc on Turing
and later and 10 bpc on Ampere and later. Reduce it to fit the TMDS
bandwidth and the 324 MHz pixel clock limit at 10 bpc.

The TMDS character rate is pixel clock * bpc / 8, so SCDC and firmware
setup must use that rate. Derive it from the programmed raster to account
for frame-packed 3D, and set the selected depth in the head and SOR.

The GCP carries the 12 bpc depth and packing phase, so send it on HDMI
enable and disable even without audio. Update only its payload bytes to
preserve SB1_CTRL.

Signed-off-by: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 96d437f72793cb16265d85dea4cb193337e4bbe1)
